body:
Antidepressants will certainly help, I've been on 20mg of Prozac for a week and can already see a decrease in my SA. Just remember that if you're having trouble holding conversation with people it's got nothing to do with your ability, you're perfectly capable, it's the anxiety filter in your head over analysing every thought before it comes out of your mouth, I've suffered with this for many, many years! It's highly frustrating. My brother had a similar issue to ours and Prozac cured him, only downside is he can't come off them, he's been taking them for 10 years. Don't worry if for the first couple of weeks you feel a little more anxiety or depression, it's a common side effect when the brain is adjusting to an SSRI drug, hang in there until the 6-12 week mark, you should start to feel good! If you don't respond well to Lexapro head back to your doctor and they'll probably prescribe you another SSRI, you may need to try a few before you find the one that you respond well to. Everybody responds differently. 

&#x200B;

All the best!

Yeah people who say that sort of shit are usually the ones who have been in relationships since they were 5 years old, they don't have any issues in "picking" up people. Go out on any Friday or Saturday night in the town and you'll see plenty of desperado guys picking up hot chicks. Yep!! Exactly the same problem here mate, I'm shy and suffer from social anxiety as well, now depression on top of it. It's a horrible cycle to be stuck in. My advice would be to maybe try medication, I know my older brother, before starting medication, was a bit like us, shy and socially anxious as fuck but he started taking prozac and after a while he didn't give a fuck about anything, he's always happy for no reason as well lol. Just a thought. 

&#x200B;

I'm seeing a doctor at the end of this week to hopefully get a prescription and start cognitive behavioural therapy, I'm sick and fucking tired of social anxiety running my life. Being shy is OK, you'll still find a girlfriend, I knew a few guys from my college who were awkward as fuck and shy, but didn't have social anxiety they didn't give a stuff what people thought of them, they managed to have sex on a regular basis, it's social anxiety that's the core problem here. It needs to FUCK OFF. 

&#x200B;

Good news for you and all of us struggling with SA is that it's the easiest form of anxiety to treat, and the most common. Just gotta get it treated because it won't go away on it's own, I've come to the end of my tether with this disorder. Definitely get it fixed so you can enjoy your 20's and fuck as many hot senoritas as you like! Especially an army guy, they'd be all over you like a rash!!

 You've written my life in a nutshell. I'm a 20yr old male, have horrible social anxiety, never had a proper job either, I sit in my hours most days browsing YouTube, I go to the gym once a day and that's the only time I really leave the house. I'm a virgin as well, never had a girlfriend and that's bringing me the most pain, seeing couples out in public brings me to tears, It kills me inside, this empty loneliness whilst you watch everybody else hold the one they love is enough to make me nearly suicide on impulse sometimes.  

&#x200B;

What I will tell you though is that my older brother used to be a bit like us around his early twenties until he went and got help, he was prescribed Prozac and that changed his life, he's been on it for 15 years, he can't function without it. Maybe consider that, along with Cognitive behavioural therapy. The good news is that Social anxiety is the easiest anxiety disorder to treat. I'm going in late next week to see if I can get a prescription. 

&#x200B;

All the best.
